      "prompt": "Scientific-educational natural-history monochrome icon for ROOT ROT. The reference leaf image sets the drawing style only. Draw one lifted small plant with two modest leaves and a natural fine FIBROUS root system. The roots must be slender thread-like branching roots throughout, with frayed truncated ends, sparse remaining rootlets and irregular decayed breaks. NO thickened storage root, tuber, bulb, swollen root, root gall or club-shaped lobe anywhere: these would wrongly suggest clubroot. Use a few missing/broken sections and rough root edges to communicate decay, not arbitrary holes. One core concept, no additional symbols, soil block, tools or text. Refined organic contours and credible botanical anatomy, single flat dark ink #30352f on actual transparent background with transparent internal spaces. No white paint, gradients or shadows. Center the whole subject with generous clear margins. A coherent silhouette readable at 32px, not a busy root diagram."
